495
00:32:53,260 --> 00:32:55,340
You know, I feel so bad.

496
00:32:55,510 --> 00:32:58,390
I haven't seen you this whole trip. Especially last night...

497
00:32:58,550 --> 00:33:02,060
Don't worry about it. It was fine. I had the best time with Rachel.

498
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:05,940
I just felt bad for you, stuck in that room working on Ross' speech.

499
00:33:06,100 --> 00:33:08,270
Actually, it turned out to be a lot of fun.

500
00:33:10,020 --> 00:33:12,320
Oh, well, at least we're both having fun, right?

501
00:33:15,280 --> 00:33:18,450
- Is it weird that it's not with each other?     - Yeah.

502
00:33:18,620 --> 00:33:20,120
A little bit, yeah.

503
00:33:25,080 --> 00:33:27,000
I think we need to talk.

504
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:31,170
Yeah, I think we do.

505
00:33:34,050 --> 00:33:35,470
About what?

506
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:41,600
- Come on, you guys, it'll be fun!     - All right.

507
00:33:41,760 --> 00:33:45,270
- I'll play if we don't keep score.     - Well, then how do we know who wins?

508
00:33:46,730 --> 00:33:51,110
- Nobody wins.     - So we're just four losers. Super.

509
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:54,900
- Well, I'm not playing with her.     - I'm out.

510
00:33:55,070 --> 00:33:56,700
- I'll play you.     - Okay.

511
00:33:56,860 --> 00:33:59,530
- You don't know what you're doing.     - She gets crazy.

512
00:33:59,700 --> 00:34:02,200
This scar? That's from Pictionary.

513
00:34:04,330 --> 00:34:06,120
I think I'll be all right.

514
00:34:06,290 --> 00:34:09,670
- You want to volley a bit for serve?     - Sure, if you want to.

515
00:34:13,550 --> 00:34:15,300
Ho!

516
00:34:16,010 --> 00:34:19,470
Oh, by the way, I'm awesome.

517
00:34:22,220 --> 00:34:24,260
Oh, dear God, there's two of them.

518
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:27,060
- You ready to play?     - Hell, yeah.

519
00:34:27,230 --> 00:34:33,070
- Did you know this about him?     - No idea. I thought he was soft like you.

520
00:34:33,270 --> 00:34:36,070
- Want to make it more interesting?     - How much you thinking?

521
00:34:36,240 --> 00:34:38,070
- Ten bucks a game?     - Make it 50.

522
00:34:38,240 --> 00:34:39,860
- I'll make it 100.     - One thousand...

523
00:34:40,030 --> 00:34:41,620
Okay!

524
00:34:42,700 --> 00:34:45,200
We'll flip to see who goes first. You got a quarter?

525
00:34:45,700 --> 00:34:48,370
No. Either of you girls got a quarter?

526
00:34:49,710 --> 00:34:52,170
Honey, try to focus the trash talk on him.

527
00:34:53,750 --> 00:34:56,800
- Monica, you call it.     - Heads. No, tails! Heads!

528
00:34:56,960 --> 00:34:59,420
- Tails.     - Oh, what are the chances?

529
00:35:04,470 --> 00:35:06,260
- Hah! My point!     - Oh, no, I don't think so.

530
00:35:06,470 --> 00:35:10,270
Standard rules: If at any time a player uses his nonracket-bearing hand...

531
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:13,440
to touch the playing surface, he or she forfeits the point.

532
00:35:17,150 --> 00:35:18,940
He was a lawyer.

533
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:23,120
All the East Coast is having beautiful weather.

534
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:25,330
In New York, it's 72 and sunny.

535
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:27,780
Oh. Weather bitch.

536
00:35:30,410 --> 00:35:31,870
It's open.

537
00:35:33,420 --> 00:35:34,630
- Hi, Joe.     - Hey.

538
00:35:35,500 --> 00:35:39,130
- What? Is everything okay?     - Charlie and I broke up.

539
00:35:39,300 --> 00:35:41,420
No. Why?

540
00:35:41,590 --> 00:35:44,390
Well, she said we have nothing in common.

541
00:35:44,550 --> 00:35:46,510
That's crazy.

542
00:35:47,390 --> 00:35:49,310
No, it's not. We have nothing in common.

543
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:52,640
- Yeah, that's true.     - Yeah.

544
00:35:52,810 --> 00:35:56,150
I mean, she should be with someone more like Ross.

545
